HOUSE(1)                       P32W Unix                        HOUSE(1)

NAME
       house - a house of lines, turned and looked at from far off

SYNOPSIS
       house [frames]

DESCRIPTION
       house draws a small house as lines (four walls, a roof
       with a chimney, a door, windows) and shows it off: one
       whole turn in 72 frames, seen from a little above; then 24
       frames going away from it and 24 coming back; and again.
       Under the window manager (wm(1)) it has a window of its
       own, 320 dots by 280, which its corner makes bigger or
       smaller; with no window manager it takes the whole of the
       video card's screen (video(4)).

       It goes on until q is typed (with its window in front,
       under wm), or its window's box is clicked, or for the
       number of frames given. With a number it does not wait
       between frames, and says at the end how long they took.

       It is the show of P8X's house, with a house of its own:
       P8X's is its graphics card's maker's.

EXAMPLES
       house
       win house
       house 120
              the whole show once, timed

       It is on the finder's Apps menu.

FILES
       /usr/src/cmd/house.c       its source
       /usr/include/g3d.h         the library it is drawn with

SEE ALSO
       cube(1), g3d(3), gfx(3), wm(1), win(1)
